 - **priority_and_order:** The failover dispatch sequence determined via `PUT /api/v1/admin/ai/providers/order` (or `PUT /api/v1/workspaces/:ws/ai-providers/order`). Providers are evaluated sequentially by priority. If a higher-tier provider encounters a 5xx error or rate limit, the router seamlessly falls back to the next active provider in the stack.
 - **token_cap_and_budgets:** Managed via `PUT /api/v1/admin/ai/budgets` (or `PUT /api/v1/workspaces/:ws/ai-providers/budgets`) across daily or monthly periods (`period_kind`). Setting `token_cap = 0` triggers a Hard AI Freeze, immediately rejecting reservations with `BudgetExceeded` and halting Sparkle completions with status `budget`. Selecting Unlimited Quota configures an internal ceiling of 10,000,000,000 tokens, recording ledger telemetry without automated cutoffs. Quick presets provide standard allowances of 1M, 5M, 25M, and 100M tokens.
 
+> [!NOTE]
+> For headless CI/CD pipelines, automated runners, and external agents authenticating via RFC 8693 token exchange without static API keys, configure Workload Identity Federation policies in the MCP Access Studio. See [Workload Identity Federation Settings](#workload-identity-federation-settings) for parameter specifications, valid formats, and subject claim examples.
